<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish Corridor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish Corridor was a strip of territory along the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a> that gave the restored Polish state access to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baltic-sea">Baltic Sea</a>. It was transferred from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a>, separating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-prussia">East Prussia</a> from the rest of Germany. Its loss was among the territorial settlements that followed the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-corridor.jpg" alt="Polish Corridor" width="320" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Space Cadet at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polish_Corridor.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
